  "director_notes": "An original solar beam: the archetype is a beam that has to soak up sunlight before it can fire, so the wind-up is the identity of the spell. Choices: (1) a long 1.15 s gather where the light visibly comes TO the caster: motes spawned on a shell spiral into the hand (sparks gather_px with swirl), green glints add the nature side, a sun glyph opens and turns underfoot, a ring of light closes in, and the whole frame brightens; (2) the release is a thick, steady lance (beam, 40-44 px) rather than a crackling laser: low wobble, a 4 Hz flicker, and two thin threads of light corkscrewing along it (spiral_count 2) so it reads as a column of light from every view; (3) the impact is a bloom, not an explosion: a soft flash, a ring of light, motes floating up and a glowing sun-mark (burn, add) over a pale sun-bleached burn. Palette is gold to white with a leaf-green secondary for the nature side. Sound: shimmer plus a low charge for the gather, a whoosh on release, a high hum for the lance, an impact and a quiet shimmer tail. Element is light; it would sit in a nature or grass type just as well."
